# SHA256 checksums for the signed focal32 trustlet, used by
# scripts/fetch-focal32-firmware.sh. Format: sha256sum ("<hash>  <file>").
# Lines starting with # are ignored.
#
# PLACEHOLDER: no real hashes are recorded yet. The blobs are not in this
# repository, and their hashes must come from a copy known to work (the
# files on a phone where focal32 already loads and enrolls), not from
# guesswork. Until all nine entries below are filled in, the fetch script
# refuses to install.
#
# To fill this in, either:
#   sha256sum /lib/firmware/qsee/focal32.mdt /lib/firmware/qsee/focal32.b0[0-7]
# on the known-good phone and paste the nine lines here (file names
# without directories), or run once with a source you trust:
#   scripts/fetch-focal32-firmware.sh --record <source>
# which writes the lines below this header (trust on first use).
#
# Expected entries (one line each, replace the placeholder with the hash):
#   <sha256>  focal32.mdt
#   <sha256>  focal32.b00
#   <sha256>  focal32.b01
#   <sha256>  focal32.b02
#   <sha256>  focal32.b03
#   <sha256>  focal32.b04
#   <sha256>  focal32.b05
#   <sha256>  focal32.b06
#   <sha256>  focal32.b07
